WEBVTT

00:00:52.636 --> 00:00:55.597
It's over eight million bucks.
That's a lot of DeNiros.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:02.229
Oh! This'a berry, berry bad!

00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:08.402
Earth's boring.

00:01:08.485 --> 00:01:09.611
I'll save us.

00:01:09.695 --> 00:01:13.782
Let's go visit my parents
at their fabulous casino in Mars Vegas.

00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:18.120
Take that, Earth!

00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:24.543
Look out, penny slots.
I've got a system.

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.462
It's to put all my money in you.

00:01:28.547 --> 00:01:32.676
Um, Zoidberg, maybe Vegas
isn't the best place for people like you.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.429
What? It's full of fat guys in sandals.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:38.849
I just mean, your money management
skills could use some work.

00:01:39.016 --> 00:01:42.477
Like, the only reason my family even
owns a casino is 'cause we've kept

00:01:42.561 --> 00:01:44.813
such a close eye on
our money for generations.

00:01:45.022 --> 00:01:46.106
You sure have!

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.649
No offense, Zoidberg,

00:01:47.733 --> 00:01:50.277
but maybe you'd be better off
if you stayed behind.

00:01:52.863 --> 00:01:56.366
Oh, yes, better. A lonely weekend

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:59.620
in my dumpster
with a jar of pennies and tears.

00:02:00.204 --> 00:02:02.080
Sounds good. See you Monday!

00:02:19.314 --> 00:02:22.067
The cops are closing in.
Better ditch the loot somewhere.

00:02:22.484 --> 00:02:24.653
Hey-yo, how about that
dumpster down there?

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:27.364
You mean the one in
that alley off 72nd Street?

00:02:27.656 --> 00:02:29.616
Yeah. What do you
think I'm pointing at?

00:02:33.829 --> 00:02:35.789
Mars Vegas, here we come!

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:58.854
God, it's Zoidberg.
I hate to bother you, but...

00:03:00.105 --> 00:03:01.899
Okay, okay, I'll shut up!

00:03:16.413 --> 00:03:18.457
This very lucky casino we own.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.834
Someone wins
one million dollar every hour!

00:03:21.084 --> 00:03:22.461
Usually it us.

00:03:23.545 --> 00:03:25.839
Thirty-three black. Everyone lose.

00:03:26.256 --> 00:03:27.591
Man!

00:03:30.302 --> 00:03:33.430
I can't help noticing a lot
of your employees are native Martians.

00:03:33.555 --> 00:03:36.099
Yeah, they a proud, grouchy people.

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:40.854
Well, they do work for minimum wage
in a land that was once theirs.

00:03:41.146 --> 00:03:44.107
Yeah, but they never made
wise use of the land.

00:03:44.233 --> 00:03:46.693
When my ancestor
Reginald Wong found them here,

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:50.113
they had no bingo parlors
and only one prostitute.

00:03:50.197 --> 00:03:51.865
Pfft. Pathetic.

00:03:53.075 --> 00:03:54.409
This here the buffet.

00:03:54.618 --> 00:03:58.705
Ooh! Perfect timing!
It's the weekly changing of the shrimp!

00:04:09.633 --> 00:04:11.843
Way up here's
the money-counting room.

00:04:11.969 --> 00:04:14.972
It's Mars' happiest place on Earth!

00:04:15.681 --> 00:04:18.600
This much money
could feed a small, starving planet.

00:04:18.767 --> 00:04:19.810
But it doesn't!

00:04:24.189 --> 00:04:25.983
I'll just reach down and get that.

00:04:28.151 --> 00:04:30.195
Something don't smell right.

00:04:31.697 --> 00:04:34.950
Don't mess with Blind Joe.
Nothing get past his sense of smell.

00:04:35.242 --> 00:04:38.829
Yeah, that's why he in here.
Guarding galaxy's most secure safe.

00:04:48.589 --> 00:04:52.050
Every day at 3:45,
we load in the daily take.

00:04:52.384 --> 00:04:54.720
This whole place is finely tuned machine

00:04:54.887 --> 00:04:57.222
for separating suckers from their money.

00:04:58.891 --> 00:05:01.393
Category five sucker now arriving.

00:05:08.692 --> 00:05:13.780
The minute you walked in the
joint I could smell you were a man

00:05:13.864 --> 00:05:15.032
Who was stinkin'

00:05:15.198 --> 00:05:20.787
A real big lobster, fresh shellfish
You give me a rash

00:05:21.246 --> 00:05:24.458
Ladies love a Decapod
With clothes made of cash

00:05:24.583 --> 00:05:26.501
Then let me get right to the point

00:05:27.586 --> 00:05:32.883
I don't boil my pot for every
Crab I see

00:05:32.966 --> 00:05:34.843
Hey, rich lobster

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:41.642
Blow your wad of cash on me

00:05:44.519 --> 00:05:46.355
Zoidberg, what are you doing here?

00:05:46.563 --> 00:05:47.773
And what's with all the money?

00:05:48.023 --> 00:05:50.943
It's my eight million dollars.
God gave it to me.

00:05:51.109 --> 00:05:55.447
Oh, come now! God didn't get to be
God by giving away money.

00:05:55.906 --> 00:05:58.492
Loosen up.
You can't take it with you.

00:05:58.575 --> 00:06:00.410
Now, I'm heading
down to the casino,

00:06:00.535 --> 00:06:02.371
and I'm taking
my money with me.

00:06:03.372 --> 00:06:07.292
This is why you never see
a poor person with millions of dollars.

00:06:10.629 --> 00:06:13.257
Eight one-million-dollar
chips, please.

00:06:13.924 --> 00:06:15.551
I think that's about eight.

00:06:15.926 --> 00:06:17.928
Everything on 34.

00:06:22.349 --> 00:06:24.476
Zoidberg, what are you doing?

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.728
I don't know.
I think it's called roulette.

00:06:30.732 --> 00:06:33.986
Thirty-four red. You win $288 million.

00:06:37.364 --> 00:06:39.074
Let it ride!

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:52.337
Thirty-four red.
Ten billion, 368 million dollars.

00:06:55.841 --> 00:06:58.093
Vodka with a sardine in it, please.

00:06:58.176 --> 00:07:01.388
In fact, vodka with a sardine all around!

00:07:03.849 --> 00:07:05.017
And let it ride!

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:10.898
Stop! At least set aside
a billion for a decent apartment.

00:07:11.148 --> 00:07:13.442
No! I'm having fun and a sardini!

00:07:25.537 --> 00:07:26.997
Fifteen black.

00:07:27.956 --> 00:07:29.291
Aw...

00:07:31.293 --> 00:07:33.295
Now that's the God I know.

00:07:33.962 --> 00:07:36.256
Zoidberg, what is wrong with you?

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:38.258
You just threw away a fortune!

00:07:38.467 --> 00:07:42.638
Eh! Easy come, easy go.
But for one brief moment,

00:07:42.721 --> 00:07:45.098
I made everybody on Mars happy.

00:07:45.182 --> 00:07:48.185
And if you ask me,
that makes me a winner.

00:07:49.519 --> 00:07:51.897
Category five loser now departing.

00:07:54.733 --> 00:07:57.110
Hey, big lobster

00:08:04.868 --> 00:08:07.871
I'll make this simple.
Our money or your life.

00:08:12.918 --> 00:08:14.253
Sardini?

00:08:19.508 --> 00:08:21.343
I'm telling you the truth, I swear!

00:08:21.552 --> 00:08:23.554
Clamps, break something
over his head.

00:08:23.845 --> 00:08:25.806
Everything in here's
already broken.

00:08:26.014 --> 00:08:28.267
Find the least broken object
and use that.

00:08:29.476 --> 00:08:32.437
This Judith Krantz novel's
only missing its frontispiece.

00:08:33.105 --> 00:08:34.231
Ow!

00:08:34.314 --> 00:08:38.318
I told you, I spent it in Mars Vegas!
All eight million dollars!

00:08:38.652 --> 00:08:41.905
He can't be lyin', boss.
Not after a Krantzing like that.

00:08:42.155 --> 00:08:44.324
All right.
Then I'm afraid we must kill you

00:08:44.408 --> 00:08:46.535
and dispose of your body
in the nearest dumpster.

00:08:46.827 --> 00:08:48.704
This one we're in seems pretty close.

00:08:55.168 --> 00:08:56.378
He's full of ink!

00:09:01.758 --> 00:09:03.552
We should have brought a gun.

00:09:06.513 --> 00:09:09.016
That was one hell
of a weekend in Vegas.

00:09:09.516 --> 00:09:11.059
Dude, where's my ship?

00:09:11.393 --> 00:09:12.769
I parked it over there.

00:09:13.353 --> 00:09:15.689
Well, I don't remember much,
but I feel fine.

00:09:17.858 --> 00:09:20.444
Oh, my God!
Amy's mirror got a tattoo!

00:09:20.694 --> 00:09:23.989
Luckily, we're prepared
for this eventuality.

00:09:25.782 --> 00:09:28.118
What's that?
A tattoo removal laser?

00:09:28.368 --> 00:09:32.205
Oh, Hermes,
you and your preposterous sci fi nonsense.

00:09:32.497 --> 00:09:36.418
No, this is simply
a translucidating ink polarizer.

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:40.422
It aligns the pigment molecules,
channeling photons through,

00:09:40.589 --> 00:09:42.925
and rendering the ink invisible.

00:09:43.091 --> 00:09:46.386
Ah. So it's less painful
than regular tattoo removal.

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:47.721
Nobody said that.

00:09:52.601 --> 00:09:54.311
The robot mafia's after me!

00:09:54.394 --> 00:09:57.189
You got to hide me,
or it's curtains for Johnny Z.

00:09:57.481 --> 00:09:59.900
Hide a giant lobster covered in ink?

00:10:00.067 --> 00:10:02.486
And how do you propose we do that?

00:10:08.784 --> 00:10:11.870
My God!
He was so saturated with ink

00:10:11.954 --> 00:10:14.623
that his entire body
structure was polarized!

00:10:14.915 --> 00:10:16.583
You mean I'm invisible?

00:10:16.792 --> 00:10:19.711
No, no, no.
Not in any sense of the word.

00:10:19.795 --> 00:10:22.422
But essentially, yes, entirely.

00:10:24.007 --> 00:10:27.886
It's no use, Zoidberg.
We're, like, 85% sure you're in there!

00:10:28.679 --> 00:10:29.846
Where is that rat?

00:10:30.722 --> 00:10:32.182
Zoidberg's not here.

00:10:32.558 --> 00:10:34.685
All right, but if you see him,

00:10:34.768 --> 00:10:36.478
give him one of these...

00:10:36.562 --> 00:10:38.230
And one of these,

00:10:38.355 --> 00:10:40.023
and not one of these.

00:10:40.566 --> 00:10:42.985
Come on, Clamps, let's go, and watch out,

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:45.571
there's some sort
of smelly air pocket over here.

00:10:50.617 --> 00:10:53.870
Well, that's that. We ain't getting
our money back from this Zoidberg.

00:10:53.954 --> 00:10:57.416
Hey, boss, this here casino
looks like it makes a lot of money.

00:10:57.624 --> 00:11:00.294
Maybe the Mafia should
get involved in the casino business.

00:11:00.627 --> 00:11:01.670
What are you, an idiot?

00:11:01.878 --> 00:11:03.005
Pretty much, yeah.

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:06.133
Then you won't notice
when I claim your idea as my own.

00:11:06.508 --> 00:11:08.635
Come on, let's go take over this casino.

00:11:11.388 --> 00:11:13.015
Fore!

00:11:16.268 --> 00:11:19.021
Mr. Wong, we have
a Mafia proposal for you.

00:11:19.104 --> 00:11:21.481
Your casino, give it to us.

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:25.027
Okay, fine, I just retire
to my fabulous mansion.

00:11:26.695 --> 00:11:29.364
Hey, boss,
ain't that the type of mansion you like?

00:11:35.662 --> 00:11:39.541
Oh, Amy, the Mafia took
everything we had.

00:11:39.708 --> 00:11:44.171
Our casino, our home,
and our collection of rare servants.

00:11:44.671 --> 00:11:47.549
Don't worry, Mom,
you can always come live with me.

00:11:47.841 --> 00:11:51.094
No, we can't.
Who do you think been paying your rent?

00:11:51.678 --> 00:11:52.930
What's rent?

00:11:58.602 --> 00:12:01.772
Okay, we're at the dump.
Where should we heave this stuff?

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:06.902
It's not a dump. It's the company housing
we built for our employees.

00:12:07.236 --> 00:12:09.446
Only place we can afford now.

00:12:09.905 --> 00:12:12.741
So just drop it here
on this bloody mattress?

00:12:22.709 --> 00:12:24.461
Thanks, Tissue Ghost.

00:12:24.544 --> 00:12:26.505
You can't afford tissue anymore.

00:12:26.588 --> 00:12:28.548
This is Walgreens brand nose paper.

00:12:29.258 --> 00:12:32.678
Zoidberg? You snuck in here
while I was taking a bath?

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:36.598
No, you snuck in here
while I was grabbing a bubble cake.

00:12:39.268 --> 00:12:42.729
Listen, Zoidberg, I owe you an apology.

00:12:42.938 --> 00:12:45.190
No, no, no. Go ahead.

00:12:45.357 --> 00:12:47.943
I was condescending to you
'cause you were poor,

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:51.863
but now I realize
it can happen to anyone. I'm sorry.

00:12:52.281 --> 00:12:56.159
I appreciate that, Amy.
Is there any way I can help, maybe?

00:12:56.618 --> 00:13:01.206
No, I don't see how...
Wait, don't see.

00:13:01.748 --> 00:13:03.166
That's how you can help!

00:13:03.792 --> 00:13:06.795
There's one sure way
to set everything right.

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:12.134
We'll use your invisibility to pull off
a daring and complex casino heist.

00:13:12.426 --> 00:13:16.054
Of course, because no one can
possibly know what I'm up to.

00:13:24.813 --> 00:13:26.440
I've summoned you to the chart room

00:13:26.565 --> 00:13:29.443
to explain how we're going to break
into the casino vault,

00:13:29.526 --> 00:13:32.279
steal millions of dollars
from under the Mafia's nose,

00:13:32.362 --> 00:13:35.782
and return the casino
to its rightful owners. Questions?

00:13:36.408 --> 00:13:39.328
Uh, how come we've never
been in this room before?

00:13:39.536 --> 00:13:41.038
I think this chart will answer that.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:43.415
Now, the heist.

00:13:44.333 --> 00:13:46.668
As you know,
the main vault is here

00:13:46.752 --> 00:13:48.587
in the counting room on the top floor.

00:13:49.004 --> 00:13:51.798
But your dad said
it's the galaxy's most secure safe.

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:56.511
Yes, but they open it
every day at 3:45 to load the take.

00:13:56.845 --> 00:14:01.016
Then Zoidberg walks right in,
because he's invisible.

00:14:01.183 --> 00:14:03.018
Well, that, that just might work.

00:14:03.185 --> 00:14:04.811
Over here with the donut.

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:06.855
But the money's not invisible.

00:14:06.939 --> 00:14:09.107
If the Mafia sees stacks
of cash floating out,

00:14:09.191 --> 00:14:11.777
won't they shoot first
and ask questions later?

00:14:12.361 --> 00:14:14.696
Not if Zoidberg eats the money.

00:14:14.863 --> 00:14:17.199
Everything he swallows turns invisible.

00:14:17.449 --> 00:14:19.034
Like so.

00:14:20.202 --> 00:14:23.080
Then later we just
retrieve it at our convenience.

00:14:23.247 --> 00:14:27.960
Hold on, that much cash would weigh...
over 300 pounds.

00:14:28.293 --> 00:14:30.295
How can Zoidberg walk out
with that much weight?

00:14:30.545 --> 00:14:33.590
And he may be invisible,
but he's not insmellable.

00:14:33.715 --> 00:14:35.759
He stinks like
the inside of a Tauntaun.

00:14:35.884 --> 00:14:37.928
Won't someone notice the stench?

00:14:38.136 --> 00:14:40.138
No, and to keep you on your toes,

00:14:40.222 --> 00:14:43.433
I'll explain why
only after the heist has begun.

00:14:50.524 --> 00:14:54.027
The key to the whole operation
is the casino's shrimp buffet.

00:14:56.154 --> 00:14:59.533
Today is Friday, the day
the week-old shrimp get hauled off,

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:01.743
so the stench should be
just strong enough

00:15:01.994 --> 00:15:03.954
to mask Zoidberg's presence.

00:15:04.079 --> 00:15:05.789
Ew.

00:15:05.956 --> 00:15:07.666
What's bringing the stank?

00:15:07.833 --> 00:15:11.587
It ain't my gambling diaper.
I just changed it. Must be the shrimp.

00:15:12.546 --> 00:15:15.549
It's working.
Zoidberg, what are you doing?

00:15:15.799 --> 00:15:17.676
Sorry, I'm just so hungry.

00:15:18.093 --> 00:15:22.681
Don't spoil your appetite.
You need to eat 300 pounds of cash salad.

00:15:23.015 --> 00:15:28.020
At precisely 3:40, the hazmat team
arrives to swap out the shrimp.

00:15:33.942 --> 00:15:37.529
Meanwhile, 10 floors above,
the vault is being opened.

00:15:50.959 --> 00:15:52.461
Something don't smell right.

00:15:52.586 --> 00:15:55.505
Shut your nose. It's just the shrimp cart.

00:16:00.844 --> 00:16:03.472
I think there was something
wrong with that rotten shrimp.

00:16:03.555 --> 00:16:05.682
Stop griping. Now get in there,

00:16:05.766 --> 00:16:08.101
and remember, eat everything in the safe,

00:16:08.769 --> 00:16:10.771
especially the little metal box.

00:16:10.854 --> 00:16:12.856
That's the most valuable thing of all.

00:16:14.524 --> 00:16:16.902
Three, two, one.

00:16:18.779 --> 00:16:24.201
Oh, no! Our cart!
We count on that for our job that we do.

00:16:24.701 --> 00:16:25.744
Pee-u.

00:16:26.078 --> 00:16:29.414
Joey, you got fingers, right?
Help me fix the lady's wheel.

00:16:37.923 --> 00:16:40.968
Once our man's inside,
we'll need to distract the Donbot

00:16:41.051 --> 00:16:43.011
so he doesn't close
the safe prematurely.

00:16:43.428 --> 00:16:46.765
You know, I think I'll close
the safe a little prematurely today.

00:16:47.099 --> 00:16:48.183
Whoa.

00:16:48.267 --> 00:16:54.064
Don't shut that door, partner.
I'm a crazy Texas robot millionaire,

00:16:54.398 --> 00:16:57.693
and I plan on losing billions
in your "casiny."

00:16:57.943 --> 00:17:00.654
Can you assure me my losings

00:17:00.737 --> 00:17:03.782
will be safe in
this here money closet?

00:17:04.116 --> 00:17:06.577
Yes. Please step aside.

00:17:08.287 --> 00:17:10.122
Four alarm chili. Four alarm chili.

00:17:10.497 --> 00:17:13.834
Hello! I'm Prime Minister
Nelson Okeke of Nigeria.

00:17:13.917 --> 00:17:16.503
I trust you received my spam e-mail?

00:17:16.587 --> 00:17:19.298
Nelson, thank God you're here, Hermes!

00:17:23.969 --> 00:17:29.224
Oh, so full.
And I still have to eat the metal box.

00:17:40.193 --> 00:17:42.738
As you can see
by my jeans and hoodie,

00:17:42.863 --> 00:17:45.365
I'm a young Internet billionaire.

00:17:45.616 --> 00:17:47.993
Help! I'm sick! I can't move at all!

00:17:48.243 --> 00:17:49.286
What was that?

00:17:49.369 --> 00:17:52.873
Un, I said "Aseeka kanamoo atall."

00:17:53.206 --> 00:17:56.960
It means, "We must
leave now in an unusual manner."

00:18:01.381 --> 00:18:03.258
I'm enjoying the casino business.

00:18:03.383 --> 00:18:05.260
You meet a lot of colorful characters.

00:18:05.928 --> 00:18:09.431
Okay, you're good to go.
Get this bubba dump out of here.

00:18:16.313 --> 00:18:18.315
Okay, push "roof" and we're home free!

00:18:21.485 --> 00:18:23.862
Zoidberg's too heavy!
The elevator's dropping!

00:18:24.112 --> 00:18:26.949
Change of plan!
We'll have to leave through the main exit!

00:18:31.411 --> 00:18:33.830
Everybody say "fresh shrimp!"

00:18:33.956 --> 00:18:36.583
That was a rough ride.

00:18:37.876 --> 00:18:38.961
Uh-oh.

00:18:41.088 --> 00:18:43.340
Look!
The shrimp cart's paying out!

00:18:50.389 --> 00:18:52.432
Keep going. We're almost outside!

00:18:52.516 --> 00:18:54.560
Zoidberg, try to just burp up singles.

00:18:57.604 --> 00:18:59.022
Blind Joe!

00:18:59.231 --> 00:19:02.401
Smell with your eyes
what I see with my nose.

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:09.283
Well, well, well,
what have we here?

00:19:10.158 --> 00:19:11.577
Seriously, what is that?

00:19:11.827 --> 00:19:15.706
It's whoever or whatever
just emptied out your safe.

00:19:16.039 --> 00:19:17.833
All right, shoot him, Blind Joe.

00:19:18.166 --> 00:19:20.043
And let this be a lesson to any other

00:19:20.127 --> 00:19:22.629
albino lobsters thinking
of robbing our casino.

00:19:26.133 --> 00:19:27.134
There ya go.

00:19:27.217 --> 00:19:29.595
Don't shoot! I have a deal to offer you.

00:19:29.845 --> 00:19:34.266
Sorry. We native Martians aren't so crazy
about deals with the Wong family.

00:19:34.558 --> 00:19:37.477
That's because
you don't know the original deal,

00:19:37.561 --> 00:19:40.063
the one my family
kept secret for centuries.

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:48.113
This is the original contract
signed by Reginald Wong.

00:19:48.405 --> 00:19:52.159
It stated that my ancestors would
hold the land for 100 years,

00:19:52.242 --> 00:19:55.037
after which it was supposed
to revert to the Martians.

00:19:55.287 --> 00:19:58.123
This casino belongs to your people!

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:05.130
But, Amy, you planned this whole
thing to get the casino back!

00:20:05.213 --> 00:20:08.634
Yes, back to its rightful owners.

00:20:09.134 --> 00:20:13.305
Now just a hold on minute.
This casino is wrongfully ours.

00:20:13.388 --> 00:20:14.473
Security!

00:20:14.556 --> 00:20:18.227
Escort the trespassers
to one of the desert's finest holes.

00:20:18.518 --> 00:20:22.022
With ironic pleasure.
Let's go, trespassers.

00:20:22.105 --> 00:20:23.440
- Hey! What? Hey!
- Those are my clamps!

00:20:23.523 --> 00:20:25.275
- Hey, what are you doing?
- Take it easy!

00:20:29.404 --> 00:20:32.741
Well, we lost the casino,
but thanks to Amy's kindness,

00:20:32.824 --> 00:20:36.245
the Martians gave us back our house.
And our other casino.

00:20:36.787 --> 00:20:39.748
So what happens to
the hero of our story, Zoidberg?

00:20:40.082 --> 00:20:41.959
Will I be invisible forever?

00:20:42.042 --> 00:20:46.713
No, only until you take a bath
and wash off this invisible ink.

00:20:47.256 --> 00:20:48.674
So, forever.

00:20:48.757 --> 00:20:52.219
Aw, come on. You can use the spa tub
in the high-roller suite.

00:20:54.179 --> 00:20:58.225
Hey, big lobster

00:20:58.308 --> 00:21:01.853
Take a little bath with me

00:21:07.025 --> 00:21:09.194
The minute you flopped in the tub

00:21:10.237 --> 00:21:13.407
I could smell you were some
red-tied shellfish

00:21:13.615 --> 00:21:15.409
A bam clam chowder

00:21:15.617 --> 00:21:17.452
A chuck mollusk

00:21:17.661 --> 00:21:19.371
A hoof... or scoop

00:21:19.538 --> 00:21:25.127
You're bottled soap for me